<!-- FOUNDER STORY -->
<section class="about-founder" id="founder">
  <div class="container">
    <div class="founder-grid">
      <div class="r-left">
        <div class="tag" style="color:var(--red);font-size:.7rem;font-weight:700;letter-spacing:.2em;text-transform:uppercase;margin-bottom:16px">The Origin</div>
        <h2 style="font-size:clamp(2rem,4vw,3.2rem);line-height:1;margin-bottom:28px;color:var(--pure)">Built by people who actually swing hammers.</h2>
        <p style="font-size:.95rem;line-height:1.75;color:var(--gray2);margin-bottom:20px">VNG didn't start in a boardroom. It started on job sites, where the people doing the work could see exactly why projects failed — not because tradespeople weren't skilled, but because nobody owned the coordination. Schedules slipped because one trade didn't know what the next one needed. Finishes were wrong because no one caught the framing tolerance. Clients got surprises because the contractor was managing their own cash flow, not their client's deadline.</p>
        <p style="font-size:.95rem;line-height:1.75;color:var(--gray2);margin-bottom:20px">VNG was built around a different idea: execution is a system, not a personality. Put the right systems in place — clear scopes, real schedules, accountable trades, structured communication — and projects deliver. Every time. Not most of the time.</p>
        <p style="font-size:.95rem;line-height:1.75;color:var(--gray2)">That is still the idea. Over a thousand projects later, nothing has changed about how we think about this. The scale has changed. The principle hasn't.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="r-right" style="display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:24px">
        <div style="background:#1e1e1e;padding:32px;border-left:3px solid var(--red)">
